{
	tags: for, indexing, sum, find,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This program replaces every instance of a given character in a character array with a specified character.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Character Arrays are particular types of matrices in MATLAB. See the class demo for more information about working this these.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>The concept of the absolute index will also be helpful in this program. See the class demo for this as well.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>To simplify this program, assume we are replacing a single character with another single character. In addition, assume the replacement is case sensitive, meaning lower case characters are different than upper case characters.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		result = P42_find_replace_char_lastname('hello cat','o',' ')
		result = 'hell  cat'
		result = P42_find_replace_char_lastname('Im referring to the latter','t','d')
		result = 'I'm referring to dhe ladder'
		result = P42_find_replace_char_lastname(['pizza ';'parrot';'lizard';'Zebra '],'z','l')
		result =
		'pilla '
		'parrot'
		'lilard'
		'Zebra '
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
